{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01EtawAFjPvdSewey9yt1jgo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Anchor is a personal productivity system for J.C. Liechty that has grown a second major surface (R&D mission control). Grounded from the project docs:\n\n**Core purpose â€” a single-folder GTD-style task manager**\n- Lives entirely in `C:\\dev\\Anchor` (no OneDrive, no syncing); **plain markdown files are the source of truth** â€” `DASHBOARD.md`, `PROJECTS.md`, `INBOX.md`, per-domain files in `domains/`, plus cancelled/saved/weekly-review archives. No database, no lock files.\n- Ships a **self-contained Python-stdlib web app** (`anchor_gui.py`) that runs persistently as the NSSM Windows service `anchor` on `http://localhost:8777`, generating the full dashboard HTML per request and writing edits straight back to markdown. A CLI mirror (`anchor.py`) does the same operations and emits a static `dashboard.html`.\n- Supports the full **task lifecycle** â€” active â†’ done â†’ cancelled / saved-for-later â†’ restored â€” with priority, energy, domain, due-date, and notes fields, all editable in the browser.\n- Ships a **daily 5 AM health check** (`anchor_healthcheck.py`, Task Scheduler) that parses every file, boots a throwaway server, exercises every endpoint and lifecycle, and writes a dated report.\n\n**Second surface â€” an R&D \"Project Cockpit\" for trio-driven development**\n- Turns each project into a per-project window for the **researchPrime â†’ Crucible â†’ Foreman** skill trio, built across four design iterations (v2 sessions/summaries â†’ v3 \"Mission Control\" â†’ **v4 \"Project Cockpit,\" built and merged to master 2026-06-13**).\n- Each lane (Research Â· Planning Â· Build Â· Deliverables Â· Grass) renders as a **tile with one honest status light** (green=working, amber=needs-you, red=crashed, grey=idle/done); clicking expands an **inline panel in place** with a balanced summary on top and a **real, resizable xterm.js terminal below**.\n- Runs work as **persistent, isolated, server-side ConPTY terminal sessions** â€” each in its own git worktree/branch, surviving disconnect, openable/attachable/killable â€” over a stdlib hand-rolled WebSocket (`pywinpty` is the *one* declared exception to the stdlib-only rule, lazy-imported in `pty_manager.py` only).\n- Adds **cached, validated, grounding-filtered summaries** (session + project), an **engine toggle** (Claudeâ†”Gemini, Gemini research-only), **per-lane doc-role maps**, a **cost/tokens/time rollup**, a **grass idea board** with promote-to-lane, and **type-aware deliverable launch** (skill/tool verify Â· service preview on a port hard-guarded â‰  8777 Â· program run Â· doc render).\n\n**Branding**\n- Presented as a **Ghost World Labs** tool \"Powered by NextGen Nuclear â˜¢,\" using the vendored `gwl-m-icon.svg` mark as favicon and masthead lockup.\n\nOne caveat on currency: the git status shows you're mid-work on branch `foreman/rnd-v4.1-cockpit` (a \"v4.1\" clean-rebuild of the project window), so the cockpit UI is actively being iterated beyond the merged v4."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4253,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":45344,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"289ef629-2d80-4f32-ae31-e6643382df2e","uuid":"13c57951-f881-4598-b79b-7aa6bb752cdb","request_id":"req_011Cc2J5u6dTD2Jnj8htgN3M"}
